{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParitySplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParitySplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barOdd_zero_oddN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barOdd_zero_oddN","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L97-L101","doc":"Sanity check that the sign is load-bearing: for a hypothetical odd-`n` atom (`sgn = +1`) the\nself-conjugate would instead have ZERO bar-odd part (feeding `g₂`) — the opposite channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barOdd_double_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barOdd_double_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L91-L95","doc":"Companion: for `sgn = −1` the self-conjugate's bar-odd part is `2·g p` (its full contribution\nlands in the bar-odd `t` channel). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barEven_zero_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.selfConj_barEven_zero_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L84-L89","doc":"**Deuteron case `n = 6`, `sgn = −1`: the self-conjugate `(3,2,1)` has ZERO bar-even part** — its\nWedderburn contribution is purely bar-odd, so it feeds the impurity `t` and NEVER the bar-even\ncoefficient `g₂`. (This corrects the sign-dropped earlier draft, which had the channel reversed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pOdd_selfConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pOdd_selfConj","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L80-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven_selfConj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven_selfConj","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L74-L78","doc":"**The corrected key fact — a self-conjugate block feeds the bar channel selected by `sgn`.**\nFor `c p = p`, the bar-even part is `(1 + sgn)·g p` and the bar-odd part is `(1 − sgn)·g p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven_conj","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L64-L72","doc":"**Covariance under conjugation** (needs `sgn·sgn = 1` and `c` an involution): the bar-even part\npicks up the sign under `p ↦ c p`. So a conjugate pair `{p, c p}` combines coherently in the\nbar-even channel with relative sign `sgn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.two_mul_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.two_mul_eq","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L59-L62","doc":"**Decomposition:** twice the block quantity is bar-even ⊕ bar-odd (independent of `sgn`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pOdd","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L56-L57","doc":"(Twice) the **physical bar-odd** part — the channel carrying the bar-odd impurity `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.pEven","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L53-L54","doc":"(Twice) the **physical bar-even** part — the channel carrying the bar-even coefficient `g₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.ConjugationParity.barImage","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/ConjugationParitySplit.lean#L49-L51","doc":"The physical **bar image** of the block quantity `g` at block `p`: conjugation `c` dressed by the\nweight sign `sgn = (−1)^{n-1}`. This is `T_λ(q⁻¹)` re-expressed in the `q`-basis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}